From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 00:36:57 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] xrun: take the Xen public headers from zephyr-xenlib


Same change as 0027 does for zephyr-dom0-xt, for the one include in xrun.

Zephyr's vendored copy of the Xen public headers under
include/zephyr/xen/public/ is gone as of upstream commit d58fbb8cfc58
(backported as 0024); zephyr-xenlib is the single source now, and its
include/xen/public/ is a byte-for-byte copy of Xen 4.21.0's. Without this the
build stops at:

  zephyr-xrun/src/xrun.c:18:10: fatal error: zephyr/xen/public/domctl.h:
      No such file or directory

Depends on 0024 (zephyr).

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5[1m]
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Pending [xen-troops/zephyr-xrun]
---
diff --git a/src/xrun.c b/src/xrun.c
index 3c23d4d..58f0de8 100644
--- a/src/xrun.c
+++ b/src/xrun.c
@@ -15,7 +15,7 @@
 #include <zephyr/sys/slist.h>
 
 #if !defined(CONFIG_BOARD_NATIVE_POSIX)
-#include <zephyr/xen/public/domctl.h>
+#include <xen/public/domctl.h>
 #endif
 
 #include <storage.h>
